34,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"It looks like our yards are a mess of old gear, and trying to switch systems during peak season is a disaster. We need something that can handle our actual reality.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings show that the board is far more lenient with recurring operating costs than capital requests, and bundled agreements have been the only way to keep renewal prices stable.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It's clear we have a problem with accountability and flexibility. Last winter's outage was a disaster because no one took ownership, and our warehouse rules change too fast for a frozen project scope.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The dispatch tool is just sitting there getting old because we can't find time to upgrade it, and that external data lift from 2018 left us with a year of mistakes!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The human cost is high; we are losing our institutional knowledge to retirement, and the depot supervisors often ignore standard training in favor of their own routines.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, if the warehouse rules change that quickly, we can't afford a rigid system. It has to be flexible enough to adapt without breaking the whole process.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, flexibility is important, but we must ensure that flexibility doesn't come with hidden, escalating costs. We need a pricing model that remains predictable even as we adapt.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, that is a fair point. However, predictability in cost is useless if the system becomes obsolete within months because it cannot evolve with our operational needs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Exactly! And if we just hire people from the outside to fix it, we might end up with more mistakes like that 2018 data lift. We need something we can actually maintain!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are all describing a fragile ecosystem. If the supervisors ignore training and the experts retire, the most sophisticated software will fail unless it is intuitive and supported by a present, guiding hand.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, that's a great point. If the gear in the yard is old and the people are stretched thin, we can't have a system that requires a PhD to run or a perfect environment to work.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, your point about maintenance is key. If we can't handle the upgrades ourselves and external teams leave a mess, we should look for a vendor that bundles support and updates into a stable, predictable cost.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, I agree on bundling, but only if it includes a single point of accountability. We cannot have another winter where four different suppliers point fingers while the system is down.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I agree! We need one person or one company to say ""I've got this"" so we aren't just staring at a broken screen while everyone else says it's not their fault!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must also consider the transition. If the system is too rigid or the training too detached from the depot's reality, the supervisors will simply revert to their old ways.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, @Mizuki, it sounds like we all want the same thing: a partner who takes full responsibility, keeps costs steady, and actually understands how messy our depots are.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. We need a solution that balances operational flexibility with financial predictability, ensuring we aren't blindsided by costs or failures after the initial implementation.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Asuka,,It seems we are in agreement. The priority must be a vendor that offers a unified support structure and a configuration process that can survive the reality of our changing business rules.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm with you all! Let's just make sure we don't pick something that's going to get old and dusty or leave us with a bunch of errors we can't fix!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We have a clear vision now. We seek a partner who respects the wisdom of the floor, supports the weary, and stands firmly behind their work. Let us see which candidates fit this mold.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
