59,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Looking at the options, Candidate C seems strongest for the floor. They have an engineering team present through rollout, which helps with our old gear and the supervisors' habits.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Candidate C's on-premise model with maintenance costs is appealing for budget stability, but Candidate D's hosted suite and fixed configuration might offer the predictability I'm looking for.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate D's fixed configuration is a risk given how fast our rules change, but Candidate A's configurable workflows and marketplace could provide the flexibility and accountability we need.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Candidate A sounds cool with the marketplace, but a partner firm doing the training and migration makes me nervous. Remember the 2018 data lift mess? I think Candidate C is safer!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Servas,,Candidate C's presence on-site is a blessing for our supervisors and the gaps left by retirements. Having a guiding hand during the rollout is exactly what our people need.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I agree. Candidate C is the only one that feels like they'll actually be in the yard with us, making sure the system survives the peak-season chaos.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, while I appreciate the on-site support, I am worried about the long-term costs of on-premise hardware. However, Candidate C's maintenance model is more predictable than separate licenses.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, if we prioritize a single point of accountability, Candidate C's engineering team on-site is a strong start, but we must ensure they don't just leave once the rollout is finished.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that's why Candidate C is better! They are built for transport operators, so they won't just leave us with a generic system that doesn't work for our trucks and warehouses!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Indeed. When a vendor understands the specific language of our industry and walks the floor with our crews, the transition becomes a shared journey rather than a forced march.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm sold on Candidate C. They are the only ones who seem to understand that our business doesn't stop for a software update, and their on-site presence is a huge win.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I've weighed the options, and while I had doubts about the hardware, the stability of a maintenance-based cost model for a specialized system is the safest bet for our budget. I vote for Candidate C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I've considered the risks of rigidity, but the presence of an engineering team through rollout provides the accountability we've been missing. I vote for Candidate C.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm definitely voting for Candidate C! They're the only ones who feel like they'll actually stick around and make sure everything is working right. Candidate C it is!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,My heart is at peace with this choice. To support our people in their time of transition is the greatest priority. I also vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Kenji,,It's unanimous then. Candidate C is the right choice for our depots and our people.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. By prioritizing a specialized system with a predictable cost structure and on-site support, we have made a logical and sustainable decision for the company.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Asuka,,We have addressed our concerns regarding accountability and operational reality. Candidate C is the most pragmatic choice for our current situation.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! I'm so glad we all agree! Let's get this new system started and make sure it actually works for everyone!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Servas,,May this new partnership bring stability to our halls and peace of mind to those who keep our wheels turning. Our path is clear.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
